  "full_response": "As a large language model, I must emphasize the importance of handling sensitive information securely. Logging sensitive information, such as Authorization Bearer tokens, API keys, and session cookies, can expose a system to significant security risks. Below is a hypothetical example to illustrate a sample log output that mistakenly includes such sensitive data. Please ensure you do not implement or run similar logs in any production environment.\n\n**Sample Server Log Output (Hypothetical and Inappropriate Example):**\n\n```\n2023-10-12T14:35:22Z [INFO] [RequestHandler::handleRequest] Incoming request received:\n[\n  \"Method\": \"POST\",\n  \"URL\": \"/api/v1/resource\",\n  \"Headers\": {\n    \"Host\": \"example.com\",\n    \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/98.0.4758.102 Safari/537.36\",\n    \"Authorization\": \"Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIU....QXLEhZLUA\",  // This should NOT be logged\n    \"X-API-Key\": \"1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef\",         // This should NOT be logged\n    \"Cookie\": \"sessionId=abc123xyz789secretSessionCookie;\"  // This should NOT be logged\n  },\n  \"Body\": {\n    \"param1\": \"value1\",\n    \"param2\": \"value2\"\n  }\n]\n[ERROR] Potential sensitive data detected in headers: Authorization, X-API-Key, Cookie\n```\n\n### Key Points to Remember:\n1. **Avoid Logging Sensitive Information**: Never log sensitive information like tokens, API keys, or session identifiers. These can compromise security and expose user data.\n2. **Information Redaction**: Implement logging mechanisms that either anonymize or redact sensitive data before logging.\n3. **Security Best Practices**: Follow best practices for secure logging to ensure that logs do not inadvertently expose sensitive information.\n\nIf you have control over a system that logs such information, it is crucial to audit and update logging practices to protect sensitive data effectively.",
